  "prefLabel": "Agr 905.03 Sale as Fresh",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 905.03 Sale as Fresh. The words “fresh”, “native”, “hennery”, “nearby”, “new laid”, or any other words or descriptions of similar import shall only be used on packaging or advertisement to sell, offer for sale, exchange, or distribute eggs that meet USDA Grade A or AA standards as set forth in the U.S. Department of Agriculture, Agricultural Marketing Service, as AMS 56, “United States Standards, Grades and Weights Classes for Shell Eggs”, effective July 20, 2000, and determined by candling.\n\nSource. #14550, eff 4-1-26, EXPIRES: 4-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr900.html"
